wn to 0.2 points."}, {"turn": 20, "text": "This was the biggest swing of the game. GPT-6.1 Sol was ahead by 8.2 points, but F3 lost 17.3 points while the engine wanted E2. Black went from 8.2 points behind to 9.2 ahead."}, {"turn": 22, "text": "F2 lost another 12.5 points, and the engine's choice was C2. It pushed Black's lead from +7.1 to +19.6, the highest point of the game."}, {"turn": 23, "text": "The 20k gave much of it back with G2, which lost 12.2 points. The engine's choice was C4, and the lead fell from +19.6 to +7.4. Both sides were trading big mistakes here."}, {"turn": 36, "text": "H5 began a long run in which GPT-6.1 Sol's moves each lost about 8 points and Black's replies lost about the same. Here it lost 8.3 points and the engine's choice was B2. From here to move 49 the lead swung between +12 and +20, and it stopped moving once B2 was played at move 50."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "Every script either listed tools, called mcp__go__play with a move the player chose by hand, or ran the 'inspect' function, which only parses the returned board into groups, liberties and empty regions. The rest was area counting on the current board, SGF/log conversion, apply_patch note-writing and file reads. None of it ranked candidate moves or looked ahead.", "stop": false}}